From 3b7682b0fa4d318e3c9683cf791fc3c6b7d8b32b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 14:51:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 059/638] flags_ui: classify AROS with desktop Unix flags

AI_PHASE: Phase 3 - single-process headless shell

AI_STATUS: flags_ui now computes a supported platform mask for AROS.

ROOT_CAUSE: GetCurrentPlatform had no AROS branch and deliberately stopped compilation with Unknown platform.

FIX_REASON: Chromium 124 has no AROS flag bit; its kOsLinux mask is already the shared desktop Unix applicability cohort used by OpenBSD.

SCOPE: components/flags_ui/flags_state.cc only.

VALIDATION: The previously failing flags_state.o target compiled for AROS.

RISK: AROS sees flags marked for the desktop Unix cohort until the flags schema gains a distinct AROS applicability bit; runtime OS identity is unchanged.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
 components/flags_ui/flags_state.cc | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/flags_ui/flags_state.cc b/components/flags_ui/flags_state.cc
index 35dea65d76..857b124e89 100644
--- a/components/flags_ui/flags_state.cc
+++ b/components/flags_ui/flags_state.cc
@@ -741,7 +741,8 @@ unsigned short FlagsState::GetCurrentPlatform() {
   return kOsCrOS;
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS_LACROS)
   return kOsLacros;
-#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_OPENBSD)
+#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_OPENBSD) || BUILDFLAG(IS_AROS)
+  // kOsLinux is the shared desktop Unix flag-applicability cohort.
   return kOsLinux;
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
   return kOsAndroid;
